{#- Dumb emitter over the computed `sdks` vars-doc list (assembled in Python
    by scripts/sunbeam_workshop/chain.py: base chain -> profile extra_sdks ->
    user sdks.add -> project-<profile>-tools). Emission contract: `- name:`
    always; `channel:`, `plugs:`, `slots:` only when present (the default
    chain carries no plugs/slots, so the golden byte-identity baseline
    holds). The YAML `#` comment block below is byte-pinned by the golden
    baseline (scripts/tests/golden/) - the authoritative chain documentation
    lives in scripts/sunbeam_workshop/chain.py and the profile-authoring
    skill. -#}
# Shared partial - the AI/tooling SDK chain every profile shares (draft D-3):
# opencode first, openchamber@latest/edge immediately after (it must follow
# the opencode SDK), gh-cli, uv@latest/stable, then the in-project
# project-<profile>-tools SDK (the `profile` jinja var resolves it).
#
# A profile whose SDKs must land between uv and the project SDK (packaging:
# orange-dev-tools@latest/edge, so its apt/squid base lands first) lists them
# in profiles/<profile>/vars.json, e.g.:
#   "extra_sdks": [{"name": "orange-dev-tools", "channel": "latest/edge"}]
#
# Include under the top-level `sdks:` key, immediately followed by the
# ssh-agent graft partial.
{%- for sdk in sdks %}
- name: {{ sdk.name }}
{%- if sdk.channel is defined %}
  channel: {{ sdk.channel }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if sdk.plugs is defined and sdk.plugs %}
  plugs:
{%- for plug in sdk.plugs %}
    {{ plug }}: null
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if sdk.slots is defined and sdk.slots %}
  slots:
{%- for slot in sdk.slots %}
    {{ slot }}: null
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
